## Pre-run elaboration (additive; no outcomes observed)

<"'!-- derives: J1.1, J1.3, J1.5, G1.1, G1.2, G1.3, G1.4 -->

Implementation review clarified these choices before the first execution:
followers'"' Committed records name the sender's preceding Committed record,
which in turn contains counted acknowledgements or an earlier learning link.
Their evidence also records their own configuration and journal at learning;
only coordinator decisions count a quorum directly. Epoch transition to
follower starts a new election timeout. Timer generations survive as scheduler
instrumentation so pre-crash timer callbacks cannot fire in a new incarnation.
Files and the containing directory are fsynced at the mailbox boundary. Local
append references survive only as observation instrumentation, never as protocol
state. A pending catch-up tracks its highest acknowledged index and rejects
replies arriving past its no-progress/final-round deadline. Configurations and
all member iteration orders are sorted.

Additional validation, predicted before execution:

* Checker fixtures: detect two coordinators in the same epoch (J1.1), a
  two-member configuration change (J1.3), a higher-epoch election missing a
  committed entry and local committed truncation (both J1.5). Permit truncation
  by a stale follower whose local commit index is zero, and permit it after
  restart resets that index. These fixtures test the current contract rather
  than retired clauses. Expected: all fixture assertions pass.
* Re-execute all 24 unmutated runs and 24 mutation runs, comparing complete
  trace bytes and results. Expected: exact equality per seed.
* Copy a shared scenario inside tmp/ under an unfamiliar filename, change its
  scenario name, and run three seeds. Expected: same safety/step results as its
  source (S3), and name-independent message/process choices.
* Run Go's vet and race-enabled tests, including real scenario runs in tests
  for byte-for-byte deterministic scheduling and synchronous trigger arming.
  Expected: no diagnostics; all three S4 seeded runs take all four actions.

No scenario, mutation or checker fixture has been executed as of this addition.
